#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:1
msgid "sbt compile"
msgstr "sbt compile"

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:4
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:7
msgid ""
"`sbt` \\[_query_ / \\] `compile`<br> `sbt` \\[_query_ / \\] `Test` / "
"`compile`<br>"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:10
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:13
msgid ""
"The `compile` task compiles the selected subprojects and their subproject "
"dependencies. Since sbt 2.x, the compiled artifacts are cached automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:15
msgid ""
"Compiling Scala code with the raw Scala compiler has been slow, so "
"significant poriton of sbt's development efforts deal with various "
"strategies for speeding up compilation."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:17
msgid "Reduce the overhead of restarting the compiler"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:19
msgid ""
"sbt server stays up in the background, allowing Scala compilation to run the "
"same Java virtual machine (JVM). Keeping the JVM warm makes compilation "
"significantly faster because it takes a long time to classload the compiler "
"and for the Just-in-Time compiler to optimize it."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:21
msgid "Incremental compilation"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:23
msgid ""
"When a source file `A.scala` is modified, sbt goes to great effort to "
"minimize the other source files recompiled due to `A.scala`'s change. This "
"process of tracking dependencies between the language constructs and "
"recompiling only the required sources is called _incremental compilation_."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:26
msgid "(Remote) caching"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:28
msgid ""
"In sbt 2.x, compiled artifacts are not only cached across the sessions and "
"builds, but can optionally be cached across different machines using Bazel-"
"compatible remote cache. See [Caching](../concepts/caching.md) for details."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:30
msgid "Test / compile"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:32
msgid ""
"Scoping the `compile` task with a configuration, like `Test / compile` will "
"compile the test sources and their source dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:34
msgid "Compilation settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:36
msgid "scalaVersion"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:38
msgid "The version of Scala used for compilation."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:41
msgid "\"3.7.3\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-compile.md:44
msgid "scalacOptions"
msgstr ""

